\p{The eager patches are relative to the main tree + the let patch (\code{\verb~|work/e1/let-tree~}); together with it they reproduce \code{\verb~|work/e1/tree2/rlvm-machine~}, except my harness change in \code{\verb~|M8Harness.java~} (the reference engine's per-unit CPU log) and my tool \code{\verb~|E1Hostile.java~}, which are not delivered. With the switch off nothing changes but the name of one condition (\code{\verb~|Machine.erStop~} is what \code{\verb~|erSeen && erDeclines~} was); the switch is not part of \code{\verb~|all~} or of the default set. To make it the default: \code{\verb~|Op.SW_DEFAULT |= SW_EAGER~} after the owners' gates (mutants, native image, timing).}
}

\subtree{
\title{9. Publication in the main tree (2026-11-24T21:57:52Z, machine jar \code{\verb~|33914d3530cf~})}

\p{The patches were rebased (three-way merge, one conflict in \code{\verb~|Reduce.k_iota3~}) on the main tree that has the fix of the wrong ACCEPTs E1-F1 .. E1-F6 (publication of 21:26:43Z, jar \code{\verb~|5945b6568177~}; [rep-machine-M5](rep-machine-M5)) and published as a publication of their own: \code{\verb~|Op~}, \code{\verb~|Debug~}, \code{\verb~|Layout~}, \code{\verb~|Machine~}, \code{\verb~|MachineSession~}, \code{\verb~|MachineEngine~}, \code{\verb~|Conv~}, \code{\verb~|Infer~} (\code{\verb~|twD~}), \code{\verb~|Code~} (\code{\verb~|targConv~}), \code{\verb~|Decl~}, \code{\verb~|Reduce~}, \code{\verb~|SWITCHES.md~}; tests \code{\verb~|SHostileEagerTest~} (new, fast group), \code{\verb~|SHostileSlowTest~} (six eager sets), \code{\verb~|M8Harness~}, the note \code{\verb~|eager-hard~} in \code{\verb~|s/manifest.tsv~}. The switch is OFF by default: with the default set the differential is what it was (Std 204, Cedar slice 11, Init 164 declines).}

\p{Gate of the published sources (frozen copy \code{\verb~|work/e1/frozen/e10~}), switch set \code{\verb~|default,eager~}, per declaration against the reference engine: tutorial 395, bugs 1,428, Cedar slice 8,418, reachability 4,413, Init 58,547, all 230 tests 17,493: DIFF-CLEAN, 0 declines; Std 101,145 of 101,146 and the 16 Mathlib slices 436,404 of 436,408 (the five units are declined by the E1-F6 rule of the fix, not by eager reduction); SOUNDNESS 0, COMPLETENESS 0. Fast group 415 tests, 0 failures. Hostile matrix, 33 switch sets (each with \code{\verb~|eager~}) x 419 rows = 13,827 judgments: the only flagged rows are the three rows of the open finding E1-F7, which is not about eager reduction (below); 21 or 22 rows per set are declined by design.}

\p{What the rebase changed: the two rows \code{\verb~|warm-eager-pair-alone-bad~} and \code{\verb~|warm-pos-across-declarations-eager-bad~} are no longer declined (\code{\verb~|eager-hard~} removed, 18 rows keep it). Their eager argument sits in a beta-redex; before the fix the machine typed the redex body under the ARGUMENT's type and so ran one comparison in the plain phase that the official kernel never runs - the recorded point with two answers. With the redex typed by its binder's declared domain (E1-F2) that comparison is gone and the deferred eager comparison fails as it does officially: the machine rejects.}

\p{Open and NOT closed by this work (board 21:3xZ / 21:4xZ, \code{\verb~|NOTES-M5.md~} "E1-F7"): the machine still accepts three exports the official checker rejects (\code{\verb~|e1-sib-proj-applied-let-pi-bad~}, \code{\verb~|e1-sib-proj-redex-pi-bad~}, \code{\verb~|e1-sib-krule-major-redex-bad~}; rows of the S manifest with the mark \code{\verb~|bind~}). The official kernel infers the type of a term it has not reduced (the raw major premise of the K rule, the struct of a stuck projection) through the declared domain of an uncontracted redex or the declared type of a let variable; the machine's type of the VALUE is only convertible with it. This is independent of the switch \code{\verb~|eager~}, and it is the reason (with S3-F1 / S3-F3) why the machine's priority stays 10.}

\p{Later the same day (22:25Z) the owner chose the "practical" policy ([owner-notes](owner-notes) note 13): the three exports above are kind T (their statement is \code{\verb~|True~}) and tolerated; they are rows with the kind mark \code{\verb~|T~} in the S manifest and the class is recorded in [rep-official-divergence](rep-official-divergence).}

\p{Numbers after the publication (jar \code{\verb~|33914d3530cf~}; 8 workers, check-only passes, \src{bench/quiet.py} windows 22:17 - 22:48Z, best / median of the later passes, \code{\verb~|default~} -> \code{\verb~|default,eager~}): native image Std 1.16 / 1.19 -> 1.02 / 1.03 s and 1.17 / 1.22 -> 1.03 / 1.04 s; cedar 1.56 / 1.59 -> 1.40 / 1.42 s and 1.56 / 1.58 -> 1.39 / 1.42 s; mathlib (one row, 3 passes) 23.92 -> 21.07 s; JVM Std 1.00 / 1.16 -> 0.82 / 0.94 s and 0.97 / 1.02 -> 0.89 / 0.99 s; cedar 1.33 / 1.65 -> 1.15 / 1.18 s and 1.25 / 1.28 -> 1.16 / 1.19 s; mathlib 20.07 -> 19.53 s. On the main tree: mutants 17,775 x (v0, default, \code{\verb~|default,eager~}): SOUNDNESS 0, COMPLETENESS 0, MACHINE-INCOMPLETE 0, WARM-ANOMALY 0; M8's gate with \code{\verb~|default,eager~}: differential SOUNDNESS 0, COMPLETENESS 0; its tier part reported the 391 units that the switch decides and the generic tier declines as differences until the harness was taught to count them (publication of 22:41Z).}
}
